<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Organisation of Western Continental Greece</h1><p class="st-meta">1821 CE – 1822 CE · capital Missolonghi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Regional revolutionary government of western mainland Greece in 1821-1822, organised by Alexandros Mavrokordatos at Missolonghi.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Western mainland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-corinth">Gulf of Corinth</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a>, rose against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in the spring of 1821. In November 1821 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phanariotes">Phanariot</a> politician <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandros-mavrokordatos">Alexandros Mavrokordatos</a> gathered local representatives at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/missolonghi">Missolonghi</a>, where they adopted a charter and created a senate to govern the region and coordinate the military chieftains.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The organisation had a senate of local notables and military leaders, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandros-mavrokordatos">Mavrokordatos</a> as president. It raised revenue, supplied armed bands and tried to restrain the chieftains, many of whom had served as armatoloi under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/missolonghi">Missolonghi</a>, a lagoon town, became the region's centre and later the scene of famous sieges.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>With the First <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-assembly-of-france">National Assembly</a> at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/epidaurus">Epidaurus</a> in January 1822 and the founding of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/first-hellenic-republic">First Hellenic Republic</a>, regional bodies were placed under the central government and were abolished during 1822. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandros-mavrokordatos">Mavrokordatos</a> became president of the national executive.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/organisation-of-western-continental-greece.jpg" alt="Organisation of Western Continental Greece" width="320" height="311"><figcaption>Image: unknown, for the el:w:Οργανισμός της Δυτικής Χέρσου Ελλάδος · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_the_Senate_of_Western_Greece,_1821.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1821 CE – 1822 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Missolonghi</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Alexandros Mavrokordatos</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Greece</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Senate of Western Continental Greece</dd></dl></aside></div>
